body_text:
## Description

Two large (chunked) uploads running at once delete each other's entry from `FileBrowserModel.uploads()`. The list never holds both, and it is empty while the second upload is still running, so the "Files still uploading" prompt that `_uploads.length` gates at `packages/filebrowser/src/model.ts:89` does not fire.

The cause is `this._uploads.splice(this._uploads.indexOf(upload))` at `model.ts:567` and `:598`. On the first chunk that entry was never pushed, so `indexOf` returns -1 and `splice(-1)` removes the last entry, which belongs to the other upload. With no delete count, a found index also removes every entry after it.

## Reproduce

Added to `packages/filebrowser/test/model.spec.ts`, under `#upload()` > `newer notebook version`, at `3a51d6d`:

```ts
it('should keep every concurrent large upload in uploads()', async () => {
  const names = [UUID.uuid4() + '.txt', UUID.uuid4() + '.txt'];
  const snapshots: string[][] = [];
  const record = () => {
    snapshots.push(Array.from(model.uploads(), u => u.path).sort());
  };
  model.uploadChanged.connect(record);

  await Promise.all(
    names.map(name =>
      model.upload(new File([new ArrayBuffer(2 * CHUNK_SIZE)], name))
    )
  );
  model.uploadChanged.disconnect(record);

  expect(snapshots).toContainEqual([...names].sort());
  expect(Array.from(model.uploads())).toEqual([]);
});
```

```
$ jest --runInBand test/model.spec.ts   # packages/filebrowser, 3a51d6d
Received array: [[], ["7075c0c2-53fe-4603-ae24-0f4907645cf0.txt"], ["7075c0c2-53fe-4603-ae24-0f4907645cf0.txt"], ["7d069912-4fc0-46b0-9a04-f8c0ad64d90b.txt"], ["7075c0c2-53fe-4603-ae24-0f4907645cf0.txt"], ["7d069912-4fc0-46b0-9a04-f8c0ad64d90b.txt"], [], []]
Tests:       1 failed, 1 skipped, 41 passed, 43 total
$ jest --runInBand test/model.spec.ts   # both splice calls replaced with ArrayExt.removeFirstOf(this._uploads, upload)
Tests:       1 skipped, 42 passed, 43 total
# not run: a browser drag of two large files
```

## Expected behavior

While both uploads run, `uploads()` lists both, and each upload removes only its own entry.

## Context

- Operating System and version: Ubuntu 24.04
- Browser and version: none, the repro is the jest suite with `ServiceManagerMock`
- JupyterLab version: main at `3a51d6d`, Node 22.23.3

Searched open and closed issues and PRs for "upload splice", "_uploads", "concurrent upload" and "Files still uploading". #12798 is the multi-file progress bar, fixed in the status bar by #12871. #20019 changes the failure branch at `:546` and `:581`, not these two lines. Draft #18431 keeps these lines and adds the same `splice(indexOf)` to a new non-chunked path, so whichever lands second needs the same change.

@krassowski the fix is `ArrayExt.removeFirstOf` on both lines plus the test above. Should it ride along with #20019, where the `:546` question is still open, or stay separate?

